id: pmc-check-generator-drift
title: Explain generator drift separately from tracker changes in changelog checks
description: Classify check failures and publish the missed ordering upgrade obligation.
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[1]: "gh:unbraind/pm-changelog#339"
created_at: "2026-11-11T08:54:50.195Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-11T21:51:54.939Z"
author: codex-changelog339-1111
acceptance_criteria: "Text and JSON classify reorder_only, rendering_changed and tracker_changed; generator drift includes the configured regeneration command; all drift checks exit 1; the 2026.11.7 upgrade action is listed; historical deliveries have release evidence; behavioral reverts fail in disposable real trackers"
comments[23]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-11T08:54:52.636Z",codex-changelog339-1111,"Read issue 339 and queue rules. Classify section-local reorder first, exact previous-renderer equality second, remaining drift as tracker_changed. Store rendering versions in the JSON receipt without changing Markdown bytes. Audit all four prior in_progress items against merged commits and release tags; close delivered historical items as explicitly requested, keeping this issue in_progress."
  "2026-11-11T09:01:06.423Z",codex-changelog339-1111,"Tracker audit complete: pmc-total-item-order delivered by #324 in v2026.11.7; pmc-stable-itemless-check by #333 and pmc-contract-changes by #328 in v2026.11.10. Closed those with actual merge timestamps and release evidence. Also closed pmc-no-empty-unreleased-337 as merged via #338 but not yet tagged. No other prior in_progress items remain. Operator facet on pmc-total-item-order supplies the 2026.11.7 regeneration action through the existing native catalog. The pinned CLI required activating the local package field registration before writing change_facets; used an ignored local extension installation."
  "2026-11-11T09:12:34.082Z",codex-changelog339-1111,"Current regression suite passes 9/9 in the disposable revert harness before and after four independent behavioral mutations. Reverting only main diagnostics fails both reorder and new-item tests (2/2 failures); changing only the check failure exit to zero fails both exit assertions (2/2); removing only the previous rendering profile fails its test (1/1); removing only the catalog facet with pinned pm fails the upgrade action test (1/1). All failures are assertions, not setup or syntax errors. Source worktree was never mutated. Typecheck and test typecheck pass; docstring gate covers 281 declarations in 52 files. No lint script is configured. Registered host checks now share the diagnosis and preserve typed exit-1 errors. Starting the full npm suite within the 45-minute gate cap; CI retains responsibility for full release coverage and Bun release gates under this task budget."
  "2026-11-11T09:13:25.759Z",codex-changelog339-1111,"Regeneration initially dropped existing dependency-only notes when the corrected releases acquired closed items: default dependency fallback applies only to itemless windows. Enable the existing --dependency-updates option in this package full-changelog script so the historical dependency notes remain alongside the newly attributed delivered items. No generator default or dependency pin changes."
  "2026-11-11T09:49:31.319Z",codex-changelog339-1111,"Full npm test passed 1072/1072 across 50 suites with zero failures, skips or cancellations in 1616 seconds. The longest lifecycle test took 1095.6 seconds, within the requested 20-minute file budget. Trailing npm flags were ignored by Node, so this run supplies no coverage evidence. Subsequent review found and fixed the previous revision dependency-selection path: the same rendering revision now flows through selection, immutable tagged heading detection and merging. The added real tracker/Git snapshot regression passes, becomes tracker_changed after a genuine new item, and fails when only the previous heading rule is reverted. Updated disposable proof: 10/10 fixed, five behavioral mutations causing seven assertion failures, then 10/10 restored. Final focused validation puts all flags before test paths and covers 40 affected files with a separate 100-percent classifier-module coverage threshold. Final-head full release and Bun gates remain CI responsibilities under the task budget."
  "2026-11-11T10:02:01.207Z",codex-changelog339-1111,"Final focused gate PASS: 871/871 tests across 37 suites in 40 files, zero failures/skips/cancellations, 788.35 seconds. Correctly ordered native coverage reports 100 percent lines, branches and functions for src/check-drift.ts only; no all-source or statement coverage claim. Every direct importer of changed modules was exercised in the earlier 1072-test full suite, including the 18-minute lifecycle stress file. Final-head full-suite/release/Bun certification remains with CI. Confirmed origin/main is still the branch starting head f231c38. Programmatic native-host regeneration fallback also retains the authoritative tracker path; transport regressions are rerunning before commit."
  "2026-11-11T10:05:52.080Z",codex-changelog339-1111,"Final transport gate passes 31/31 (the ten new regressions plus registered extension tests), with zero failures/skips/cancellations. Typecheck, test typecheck and docstring gate pass again (281 declarations, 52 files); no lint script exists. The latest pinned pm test --run --match prove-check-generator-drift-revert.ts --progress passes in 47.5 seconds: fixed 10/10, five independent mutations producing seven assertion failures, restored 10/10. All behavioral mutation work remains in disposable copies. The CLI refused editing a linked test command identity as designed; atomically replaced the entry through its prescribed remove/add recovery and linked the exact successful focused and transport commands. No pm CLI/SDK defect or out-of-scope code blocker was found. Keep this item in_progress for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-11-11T10:09:51.128Z",codex-changelog339-1111,"Opened PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-changelog/pull/341 with implementation commit b34a05c. Local evidence: full npm 1072/1072 before the final selection edge case; final affected suites 871/871 across 40 files with classifier-only 100-percent lines/branches/functions; final transport 31/31; pinned behavioral proof fixed 10/10, five mutations causing seven assertion failures, restored 10/10. Typecheck, test typecheck, build, docstrings and changelog/link check passed. No lint script is configured. Full final-head release coverage, full-suite CI and Bun gates are pending and are not claimed as approval. Releasing this own claim for orchestrator verification; the item remains in_progress. The final receipt commit will preserve all historical audit prefixes and rerun the changelog after these tracker writes."
  "2026-11-11T11:53:34.227Z",codex-changelog339-1111,"Resumed the scoped review round at 643e0e1 with a clean worktree. Read all nine unresolved threads and all nine full comments/diff hunks, with pagination complete. Classes: parsed-model regeneration commands including canonical host flags, stdin and cross-platform quoting; rendering-version evidence plus complete multiline entry blocks; native upgrade declarations for the two 2026.11.10 rendering changes; portable behavioral proof baselines. Preserve the accepted classifier architecture, append-only tracker history, and prior gate evidence. Do not reply to or resolve review threads; provide the per-thread fix table for the orchestrator."
  "2026-11-11T12:26:22.032Z",codex-changelog339-1111,"Review classes A-D implemented. Parsed-model commands keep canonical flags and equals-form pm-arg pairs, ignore embedding argv, retain the native tracker path once, provide PowerShell plus lossless argv, and require the original stdin pipe without advertising a standalone command. Upgrade attribution requires an exact previous-renderer match AND different declared revisions; unproved/current-version reorders explain timestamp or manual edits. Blank-separated details remain entry units. Added distinct 2026.11.10 contract and empty-pending upgrade facets and a rendering-change tag/catalog invariant. Proof baseline chooses a pinned merge base or working-tree source and owns its diagnostic mutation, avoiding no-op fallback. Initial gates: 16/16 regression tests, classifier-only 100 percent lines/branches/functions, 3/3 baseline selection controls; 15 independent behavioral mutants caused 17 assertion failures followed by 16/16 restored controls. Both requested B regressions fail on their function-only mutations. Full source-clone/archive proof and all importing test files are next; prior completed delivery hygiene is preserved."
  "2026-11-11T13:17:04.718Z",codex-changelog339-1111,"Scoped review round PASS: complete npm-test-equivalent build/build:test and all 57 test files ran with flags before paths, two workers, per-file 1200-second timeout and overall 2700-second cap. Result 1083/1083 across 50 suites, zero failures/skips/cancellations, 1963.27 seconds; the longest lifecycle case was 1177.06 seconds. New focused regressions pass 16/16; classifier-only coverage is 100 percent lines/branches/functions. Portability gate passes 4/4, executing the complete proof in a fresh single-branch clone and a source archive; those also pass within the full run. Refreshed three baseline controls verify the additional ancestor-checkout and inherited-Git-context guard. Latest pinned pm proof run passed 16 controls, 15 independent mutations with 17 expected assertion failures, and 16 restored controls. Both B function-level reverts fail their new regressions; A command/pipe/Windows/alias, both C catalog actions, and D baseline prerequisite each have mutation evidence. The new copy/run fixture initially exposed a missing manifest in the disposable package; copied that manifest and the final runs pass. No pm CLI/SDK defect was found. Typecheck, test typecheck, build, and docstrings pass (283 declarations, 53 files); no lint script exists. Win32 quoting/argv is unit-tested; actual copied commands were executed on POSIX and the native pm host, with no live Windows claim. All nine full comments and diff hunks were read with complete pagination; no thread replies or resolutions were sent."
  "2026-11-11T13:17:05.658Z",codex-changelog339-1111,"Thread mapping for the orchestrator: PRRT_kwDOSfkApc62HuoO parsed-model host-safe commands; PRRT_kwDOSfkApc62Huoc stdin input preservation; PRRT_kwDOSfkApc62IIZM contract upgrade facet; PRRT_kwDOSfkApc62IIZX empty-pending upgrade facet; PRRT_kwDOSfkApc62IIZe portable baseline and clone/archive proof; PRRT_kwDOSfkApc62IIZl complete multiline entry units; PRRT_kwDOSfkApc62IIZp PowerShell form plus argv; PRRT_kwDOSfkApc62IIZz distinct-version and previous-rendering evidence; PRRT_kwDOSfkApc62IIZ7 registered flag normalization. All fixes and their pm evidence will be committed together and pushed to existing PR 341. Release this own claim while leaving the item in_progress for orchestrator verification; CI and reviewer status remain separate from local test evidence."
  "2026-11-11T14:11:18.011Z",codex-changelog339-1111,"Final scoped round on accepted head 67ed925: fetched all three new review threads and their complete comments/diff hunks (PRRT_kwDOSfkApc62Mhts, PRRT_kwDOSfkApc62Mhtv, PRRT_kwDOSfkApc62Mht1). Preserve accepted nine-thread fixes. Add prepend-cleanup operator action and invariant coverage, document file-output versus stdout checks, and retain pre-2026.11.7 ordering behind the shared rendering profile table with upgrade-version evidence. Validate real trackers and isolated behavioral reverts, then bounded gates and same-branch push; do not close own item."
  "2026-11-11T14:18:04.583Z",codex-changelog339-1111,"Prepend cleanup has no published release yet (latest release remains v2026.11.10). Added rendering-change tag and pending operator upgrade action to pmc-no-empty-unreleased-337 without inventing a delivery release. Its native-tracker invariant previews publication and verifies no published obligation exists yet. Initial focused run exposed that catalog queries rejected genuinely absent release attribution; defer those pending declarations while retaining the existing refusal for explicit invalid release strings. Retained the exact historical comparator in the rendering profile table, wired it through ordinary/release-window/breaking-entry sorting, and proved old committed bytes diagnose rendering_changed with 2026.11.7 in both CLI and extension. Documented stdout precedence and file-output-only drift exit guarantee."
  "2026-11-11T14:20:50.109Z",codex-changelog339-1111,"Pinned linked behavioral proof PASS (98.18 seconds): 19 fixed controls, 20 independent mutations causing 22 expected assertion failures, 19 restored controls. This retains all accepted nine-thread proofs. New final-round proofs independently remove the pending prepend-cleanup catalog action, retained old-order comparator, historical match, absent-release deferral, and qualified documentation; each fails its regression once as an assertion failure. The entire proof uses disposable packages/native trackers with append-only catalog mutation history; the package source was never reverted. Earlier focused real tracker/catalog gate passed 23/23 across two files, zero failures/skips/cancellations; final bounded 12-file gate is running with two workers and classifier-only coverage, isolated HOME/Git config, and 20-minute caps."
  "2026-11-11T14:29:10.716Z",codex-changelog339-1111,"Final scoped gate PASS: 343/343 tests, 23 suites across 12 files (check-generator-drift, check-diff, cli-coverage, cli-regression, cli-tracker-target, extension, generator, generator-coverage, generator-redos, consumer-upgrades, stable-section-order, proof-baseline), zero failures/skips/cancellations. Node duration 454.05 seconds; bounded process wall time 468.63 seconds, all within the 20-minute caps and two-worker limit. Classifier-only coverage is 100 percent lines/branches/functions; no all-source claim. Complete 20-mutation proof passes in both a fresh single-branch clone and a source archive (282.35 seconds combined), preserving the accepted portability fix. Typecheck, build, build:test and docstrings pass (285 declarations, 53 files); no lint script exists. Three new threads, three complete comments and three diff hunks read with complete pagination; no replies/resolutions sent. Record all final fixes and pm history in one same-branch commit, release own claim while retaining in_progress, then regenerate/check changelog after these last tracker writes. Full-suite CI is separate from this requested short-round gate; prior-head 1083-test receipt is not a current-head full-suite claim. No new pm CLI/SDK defect blocked this round."
  "2026-11-11T21:16:32.332Z",codex-changelog339-1111,"Round 4 starts from accepted head 4c58cfa. Read six new inline findings in full plus the latest CodeRabbit review body and its outside-diff finding (seven findings total); complete thread/comment pagination. Merged origin/main v2026.11.11 in a standard merge commit; only conflict was the generated extension map, rebuilt from merged source. Took main changelog and regenerated. No tracker conflicts or pending merge receipts; health retains pre-existing schema/provenance warnings, with no history repair. Main now supplies the published delivery version for the pending prepend-cleanup action. Scope: ordered historical profile comparisons and empty-section compatibility, complete source-derived mutation proofs, local guidance without CI-only flags, package tracker links, blank-release normalization, and release attribution for the outside-diff finding."
  "2026-11-11T21:21:35.003Z",codex-changelog339-1111,"Publication evidence correction: main 9b2c446 is release metadata, and the GitHub v2026.11.11 release lookup is absent; npm independently confirms published pm-changelog 2026.11.11 with registry integrity. Do not equate the GitHub metadata commit with publication evidence. The outside-diff gap is being fixed in release preparation: only after the job selects an explicit stable delivery version, attribute delivered rendering-change items that lack a normalized release, and commit native item/history metadata in the same release PR. Current pending metadata is not assigned speculatively during this review."
  "2026-11-11T21:26:42.244Z",codex-changelog339-1111,"Outside-diff resolution: inspected the published npm pm-changelog 2026.11.11 archive and verified its dist/generator.js contains the prepend cleanup. Recorded that actual delivery release on pmc-no-empty-unreleased-337 using pinned pm; this is publication evidence independent of the missing GitHub release page. Future pending declarations are attributed by the new release-preparation script only after the workflow selects a stable delivery version, with native items/history explicitly staged in the release metadata commit. No publication or tag was performed in this task."
  "2026-11-11T21:28:15.283Z",codex-changelog339-1111,"Comparison and guidance regressions PASS 22/22; auxiliary native-tracker/proof-runner regressions PASS 3/3. Retained output profiles include 2026.11.10, 2026.11.7 and 2026.11.6, automatically ordered newest first; old include-empty Unreleased behavior is shared in the existing selection pipeline. The empty-output golden was captured by executing the published npm 2026.11.6 CLI against a real non-git tracker; only text output and public integrity provenance are tracked. Exact older matches name the compared rendering version. CI-only reporting flags are omitted from both parsed option snapshots and final guidance, while blank releases use the same direct/metadata field normalization as grouping. Package catalog docs link every action to its native item and explicitly require a package checkout root. Shared proof collection reports every mutation and restored control before aggregate failure; source seams are derived and missing/ambiguous seams fail loudly."
  "2026-11-11T21:33:03.189Z",codex-changelog339-1111,"Drift proof PASS: 22 fixed controls; 30 independent mutations cause 32 expected assertion failures; 22 restored controls; all 32 proof cases reported and passed in 121.05 seconds. The first empty-Unreleased linked run was incomplete: I omitted its separate runner timeout metadata, so the pinned host applied its documented 120-second default despite the shell timeout wrapper. All four mutation receipts appeared, but the restored control was interrupted. No children remain. Corrected timeout_seconds to 1200 and rerun with explicit --timeout 1200; retain the incomplete receipt rather than presenting it as a pass. This is runner configuration, not an SDK gap."
  "2026-11-11T21:51:52.703Z",codex-changelog339-1111,"Round 4 final gate PASS: 385/385 tests across 17 files and 29 suites, zero failures/skips/cancellations. Node duration 595.17 seconds, bounded process wall time 609.21 seconds; two workers and 1200-second file/process caps. Includes generator/check-drift/CLI/extension/consumer-upgrade files, empty-Unreleased, release-publication/sync-version, new proof-runner/release-attribution tests, and complete portability proofs in both a fresh single-branch clone and a source archive. Classifier-only coverage is 100 percent lines/branches/functions; no all-source claim. Typecheck, build, build:test, docstrings (56 files, 288 declarations) and publish-attestation audit pass; no lint script or actionlint executable is configured. Pinned drift proof now has 23 fixed controls, 31 mutations with 33 expected assertion failures, 23 restored controls, all 33 cases reported. Pinned empty-Unreleased proof passes 9 fixed, four mutations with 14 expected failures, nine restored, all six cases reported in 157.21 seconds after the explicit timeout correction. Preserve the incomplete initial timeout receipt. The final code is unchanged during these gates; full npm/Bun release certification remains with current-head CI."
  "2026-11-11T21:51:53.845Z",codex-changelog339-1111,"Round 4 thread mapping: PRRT_kwDOSfkApc62Nvho historical empty-section profile and newest-first table comparisons; PRRT_kwDOSfkApc62Nvhy all mutation/restored cases collected before aggregate failure; PRRT_kwDOSfkApc62OIap package checkout instructions and direct native tracker links; PRRT_kwDOSfkApc62OIaw source-derived seams with missing/ambiguous seam refusals; PRRT_kwDOSfkApc62OIa1 exclude CI reporting flags from local guidance; PRRT_kwDOSfkApc62OIa6 blank-release normalization shared with grouping. Latest CodeRabbit outside-diff finding is fixed by verified npm 2026.11.11 attribution for pmc-no-empty-unreleased-337 and future release-job attribution/staging with independent native-tracker, helper-function, workflow-stage and metadata reverts. Six full inline threads/comments/diff hunks plus one full latest review body/outside finding were read; no replies or resolutions sent. Merge commit 17ad007 retains origin/main ancestry with no rebase. Commit all code, generated output, docs and native pm evidence together, release own claim while leaving own item in_progress, regenerate/check after these writes, then push the same PR."
